DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
45822::$$$message_0442_0000_0000$$$::"We are legion, yet one... One, yet legion."::
45823::$$$message_0442_0000_0001$$$::"Pine, plum, cherry, wisteria, iris. The phoenix in the paulownia, the moon over the monk, the red of Miyoshino in boar, deer, and butterfly..."::
45824::$$$message_0442_0000_0002$$$::"It is I, Asako: the quickest Hassan to pick up hanafuda among the Hundred Personas."::
45825::$$$message_0442_0000_0003$$$::"In this tutorial, I would like to teach you about hanafuda and the unique rules of [font italic=true]Rise! Operation Super Space-Time Tiger&Shorts Hanafuda[font italic=false]."::
45826::$$$message_0442_0000_0004$$$::"Thank you for your time today."::
45827::$$$message_0442_0000_0005$$$::"I should note that my outfit [hfwww layer=2]is neither a Brazilian swimsuit, pectoral posture support, nor a Middle Eastern belly dancer costume."::
45828::$$$message_0442_0000_0006$$$::"My assistant will be another Hassan, Mini Assassin."::
45829::$$$message_0442_0000_0007$$$::"..."::
45830::$$$message_0442_0000_0008$$$::"...Mini-Asa here is a fearsome Hassan all her own, capable of delivering an instant cat-punch to painstakingly built hanafuda card towers."::
45831::$$$message_0442_0000_0009$$$::"She does not speak due to her tragic past... But that won't pose a problem. Show her your respect."::
45832::$$$message_0442_0000_0010$$$::"...Miss Asako, I need to go potty."::
45833::$$$message_0442_0000_0011$$$::"I told you to go before we start! Oh...[wvl][hffacechg2 chara=アサ子 face=哀 pos=winner time=400 textclear=0][hfsweat layer=2 ox=-150 oy=30] So now you talk? Breaking character already?"::
45834::$$$message_0442_0000_0012$$$::"F-fine, then. It's hardly an issue compared to that famished king's Cambrian explosion..."::
45835::$$$message_0442_0000_0013$$$::"Miss Asako..."::
45836::$$$message_0442_0000_0014$$$::"Go already. Make sure you wash your hands, okay? Don't just wipe them on your clothes."::
45837::$$$message_0442_0000_0015$$$::"Okay! (totters away)"::
45838::$$$message_0442_0000_0016$$$::"Now, where were we?"::
45839::$$$message_0442_0000_0017$$$::"Hanafuda is a card game played with 48 cards illustrated with flora representing the twelve months."::
45840::$$$message_0442_0000_0018$$$::"I'm told it's based on the kai'ooi shell-matching game from the Heian period and Tenshou karuta, which was imported from the Portuguese and popularized during the Edo period..."::
45841::$$$message_0442_0000_0019$$$::"Anyway, go read a wiki if you want to know more."::
45842::$$$message_0442_0000_0020$$$::"Wicky?"::
45843::$$$message_0442_0000_0021$$$::"Welcome back. Whoa, that was fast! [wvl][hfwww layer=2]W-w-we'll keep going, then. All right?"::
45844::$$$message_0442_0000_0022$$$::"Yeah."::
45845::$$$message_0442_0000_0023$$$::"First, we'll cover the most well-known way to play hanafuda: Koi-Koi. That's the basis of [font italic=true]Rise! Operation Super Space-Time Tiger&Shorts Hanafuda[font italic=false]."::
45846::$$$message_0442_0000_0024$$$::"Koi-Koi is a 2-player game. Each person plays cards and tries to build scoring hands."::
45847::$$$message_0442_0000_0025$$$::"Hands are worth various amounts of points. Players repeat matches until the victor takes all points from the other player."::
45848::$$$message_0442_0000_0026$$$::"At least remember this common wisdom, even if you have to nap on it. Got it?"::
45849::$$$message_0442_0000_0027$$$::"(Trembles)"::
45850::$$$message_0442_0000_0028$$$::"Aww. You're cute, so I'll forgive you. It's okay, you can learn as you play."::
45851::$$$message_0442_0000_0029$$$::"Now, I'll explain the topics in order."::
45852::$$$message_0442_0000_0030$$$::"The first step is to determine who the dealer is. Each player draws a card, and whoever draws the earliest month is the dealer and goes first."::
45853::$$$message_0442_0000_0031$$$::"Okay, Mini-Asa. If we draw May and November, who goes first?"::
45854::$$$message_0442_0000_0032$$$::"...Asako, because you're my mommy."::
45855::$$$message_0442_0000_0033$$$::"Whoa whoa WHOA I am not your mother. May goes first, right?"::
45856::$$$message_0442_0000_0034$$$::"...May?"::
45857::$$$message_0442_0000_0035$$$::"Yeah, yeah! Whoever draws May is the dealer, so they go first."::
45858::$$$message_0442_0000_0036$$$::"Once you know who the dealer is, it's time to deal out the cards. As for how many to deal..."::
45859::$$$message_0442_0000_0037$$$::"Each player is dealt 8 cards for their hand. 8 cards are placed face-up on the field. The remaining 24 go face-down to form the deck."::
45860::$$$message_0442_0000_0038$$$::"Once that's done, you're ready to play. So far, so good."::
45861::$$$message_0442_0000_0039$$$::"Too easy."::
45862::$$$message_0442_0000_0040$$$::"Too easy."::
45863::$$$message_0442_0000_0041$$$::"Now the game starts. The dealer goes first."[skip_next_tag][br]::
45864::$$$message_0442_0000_0042$$$::"Play one card from your hand onto the field."::
45865::$$$message_0442_0000_0043$$$::"If there are any field cards of the same month, they become yours. The cards you acquire are set aside and don't go directly into your hand."::
45866::$$$message_0442_0000_0044$$$::"Next, a card is played from the deck onto the field. [wvl canskip=false time=600][fg left=160 index=8000 top=5 time=500 storage=hf_tutorial_プレイヤーターン5 laye=4]If there are any cards of the same month, they become yours."::
45867::$$$message_0442_0000_0045$$$::"In other words, if you're lucky, you could acquire up to 4 cards in a single turn. But you might gain nothing at all, too."::
45868::$$$message_0442_0000_0046$$$::"If none of the cards from your hand or the deck share the same month as the cards on the field, they all remain on the field."::
45869::$$$message_0442_0000_0047$$$::"...Is it over yet?"::
45870::$$$message_0442_0000_0048$$$::"No, not yet."::
45871::$$$message_0442_0000_0049$$$::"Then we destroy them?"::
45872::$$$message_0442_0000_0050$$$::"You won't get any points by destroying or killing the opponent."::
45873::$$$message_0442_0000_0051$$$::"Simply acquiring cards doesn't earn you any points. You have to combine them into scoring hands."::
45874::$$$message_0442_0000_0052$$$::"There are a variety of combinations."::
45875::$$$message_0442_0000_0053$$$::"It's a catalog."::
45876::$$$message_0442_0000_0054$$$::"If you have any scoring hands, or are one card away from one, they'll be displayed at the bottom of the screen."::
45877::$$$message_0442_0000_0055$$$::"Once you complete hands using the cards you've acquired, you can call the match."::
45878::$$$message_0442_0000_0056$$$::"...Do you have to?"::
45879::$$$message_0442_0000_0057$$$::"Nope, you can keep playing. Calling the match with a weak hand could actually put you at a disadvantage."::
45880::$$$message_0442_0000_0058$$$::"In this case, you can 'Koi-Koi' without calling the match."::
45881::$$$message_0442_0000_0059$$$::"Tweet tweet tweet, koi koi koi koi!"::
45882::$$$message_0442_0000_0060$$$::"Spin round and round! (makes a racket)"::
45883::$$$message_0442_0000_0061$$$::"R-right..."::
45884::$$$message_0442_0000_0062$$$::"Koi-Koi can be the right move if you're aiming to build high-scoring hands and want to deal more damage to the opponent."::
45885::$$$message_0442_0000_0063$$$::"If you can't call the match because you don't have a hand, or you decide to Koi-Koi, the other player's turn begins. Everything else is done the same way, in the same order."::
45886::$$$message_0442_0000_0064$$$::"Both players continue to alternate turns until someone calls the match or runs out of hand cards."::
45887::$$$message_0442_0000_0065$$$::"If you run out of hand cards without completing a scoring hand, the cards are re-dealt and the game starts over. This will happen as long as both players have points."::
45888::$$$message_0442_0000_0066$$$::"Now, in Koi-Koi, the rule is that points are counted in increments of 'mon'[line len=2]one mon, two mon..."::
45889::$$$message_0442_0000_0067$$$::"Each player begins the game with 12 points, and the player who gets the match called on them loses points according to the challenger's hand."::
45890::$$$message_0442_0000_0068$$$::"The game ends once a player has zero points. The player who still has points remaining wins."::
45891::$$$message_0442_0000_0069$$$::"...If the player who isn't the dealer manages to create a hand with the last card they gain, the match will automatically be called. Be aware of that."::
45892::$$$message_0442_0000_0070$$$::"Is that understood?"::
45893::$$$message_0442_0000_0071$$$::"Too easy."::
45894::$$$message_0442_0000_0072$$$::"Too easy."::
45895::$$$message_0442_0000_0073$$$::"Now to discuss the cards themselves. In addition to the months, each card has four types:"::
45896::$$$message_0442_0000_0074$$$::"Ko, Tane, Tan, and Kasu."::
45897::$$$message_0442_0000_0075$$$::"There are 5 Ko cards with vivid illustrations corresponding to January, March, August, November, and December."::
45898::$$$message_0442_0000_0076$$$::"You can use Ko cards to create high-scoring hands ranging from Sanko to Goko."::
45899::$$$message_0442_0000_0077$$$::"Tane cards are illustrated mainly with animals."::
45900::$$$message_0442_0000_0078$$$::"You can create hands such as Tane or Inoshikacho with them."::
45901::$$$message_0442_0000_0079$$$::"Kitty, deer, butterfly?"::
45902::$$$message_0442_0000_0080$$$::"No cats here. Sorry!"::
45903::$$$message_0442_0000_0081$$$::"Moving on... The Tan cards have red and blue ribbons on them. They can form the Tan, Akatan, and Aotan hands."::
45904::$$$message_0442_0000_0082$$$::"There are three blue Ribbon cards. However, there are 3 red Ribbon cards with text, and 4 red Ribbon cards without text, for a total of 7."::
45905::$$$message_0442_0000_0083$$$::"Cards that are neither Ko, Tane, nor Tan cards fall under the Kasu category."::
45906::$$$message_0442_0000_0084$$$::"Even among us, there are those who cannot grasp their merits..."::
45907::$$$message_0442_0000_0085$$$::"Even Kasu cards can form Kasu hands."::
45908::$$$message_0442_0000_0086$$$::"Only a fool might try to win a battle one point at a time... a fool...[wvl canskip=false time=400][hffacechg2 chara=アサ子 face=哀 pos=winner time=400 textclear=0][hfsweat layer=2 ox=-150 oy=30][hfangry layer=2]Zayd... I'm sorry, so sorry..."::
45909::$$$message_0442_0000_0087$$$::"That should do for the cards. Now let's move on to the hands."::
45910::$$$message_0442_0000_0088$$$::"There are 12 scoring hands in Koi-Koi. Essentially, you can create hands by collecting the same type of card."::
45911::$$$message_0442_0000_0089$$$::"Collect Ko cards to form the Sanko, Shiko, or Goko hands."::
45912::$$$message_0442_0000_0090$$$::"Ame, the 'Rain' card, cannot be part of Sanko, and Ameshiko is worth only 7 points, instead of 8."::
45913::$$$message_0442_0000_0091$$$::"Ko cards can also be combined with a Tane card to form the Hanamizake and Tsukimizake hands, as you can see."::
45914::$$$message_0442_0000_0092$$$::"Next is Inoshikacho. You can add other Tane cards to this hand to achieve an even higher score. It isn't easy, though."::
45915::$$$message_0442_0000_0093$$$::"The Akatan and Aotan hands can also be combined with other Tan cards for extra points."::
45916::$$$message_0442_0000_0094$$$::"Akatan requires Tan cards with text on them, so be careful. If both Aotan and Akatan are present, they are worth a total of 10 points."::
45917::$$$message_0442_0000_0095$$$::"Collect all five Tane cards to form the Tane hand."::
45918::$$$message_0442_0000_0096$$$::"Similarly, collecting any five Tan cards will form the Tan hand, even if you lack enough for Aotan or Akatan."::
45919::$$$message_0442_0000_0097$$$::"For each additional card, you gain 1 extra point. With 6 cards, you get 2 points, and 7 cards give 3 points." ::
45920::$$$message_0442_0000_0098$$$::"Finally, you can form a Kasu hand by collecting 10 Kasu cards. It's only worth 1 point..."::
45921::$$$message_0442_0000_0099$$$::"That covers the rules of Koi-Koi. Now I'll explain how the main game [font italic=true]Rise! Operation Super Space-Time Tiger&Shorts Hanafuda[font italic=false] works."::
45922::$$$message_0442_0000_0100$$$::"Select 'Rules' from the title screen to view detailed conditions for creating hands."::
45923::$$$message_0442_0000_0101$$$::"Select 'Options' from the title screen to adjust your play environment."::
45924::$$$message_0442_0000_0102$$$::"'View Hands' and 'View Cards' should be helpful as you play."::
45925::$$$message_0442_0000_0103$$$::"Thanks for bearing with me. Now let's talk about Noble Phantasms, the most unique aspect of [font italic=true]Rise! Operation Super Space-Time Tiger&Shorts Hanafuda[font italic=false]."::
45926::$$$message_0442_0000_0104$$$::"Noble Phantasms are ultimate moves unique to each character in this game."::
45927::$$$message_0442_0000_0105$$$::"Each team has MP that can be spent to activate Noble Phantasms, which can quickly turn the tide of battle."::
45928::$$$message_0442_0000_0106$$$::"Acquire Ko cards to increase your MP. You can't just have them in your hand. You need to play them on the field to collect them."::
45929::$$$message_0442_0000_0107$$$::"Additionally, each team has certain cards that increase MP, but I'll keep that a secret for now."::
45930::$$$message_0442_0000_0108$$$::"Noble Phantasms have wide-ranging effects. Select 'NP Details' from the 'Options' menu to learn more."::
45932::$$$message_0442_0000_0110$$$::"What about Mini-Asa's Noble Phantasm?"::
45933::$$$message_0442_0000_0111$$$::"Hmm. We don't have one. Actually, we're only in the tutorial this time."::
45934::$$$message_0442_0000_0112$$$::"Weeeh... Why did Zayd die so quickly..."::
45935::$$$message_0442_0000_0113$$$::"I-I'm sure he'll get his time to shine in the fifth war! Look forward to our exploits in [font italic=true]Fate/stay night![font italic=false]"::
45936::$$$message_0442_0000_0114$$$::"Let's try out a practice game, then."::
45937::$$$message_0442_0000_0115$$$::"Okay!"dk�